Google Chrome for Testing
=========================

This file is written by hand. It is the only entry in this tree that is not a
copy of an upstream license text, because the thing it covers ships without one.

What is fetched
---------------

`chrome-win64.zip` from the Chrome for Testing channel, resolved through
https://googlechromelabs.github.io/chrome-for-testing/last-known-good-versions-with-downloads.json

Demido Studio fetches this only when the machine has no browser it can already
drive. See `docs/rules/setup.md` section 6. It is never bundled with Demido and
never redistributed by it: the fetch is made by the user's own machine, from
Google, at set-up.

License
-------

Google Chrome Terms of Service, at https://www.google.com/chrome/terms/

This is proprietary software. It is the only proprietary item in Demido's
runtime manifest, and the only one that is not open source.

Why there is no license text below
----------------------------------

All 308 entries of the archive were listed on 2026-09-05 and none of them is a
license, a notice, or a terms file. Chrome carries its own credits inside the
binary: they are readable at `chrome://credits` from a running Chrome, and
nowhere else.

A user who wants the full third-party credits for the Chrome that Demido fetched
should open it and visit `chrome://credits`. Demido's own credits surface says
so, rather than reproducing a text that does not exist on disk.

Not affiliated
--------------

Google Chrome and Chrome for Testing are products of Google LLC. Demido Studio
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google.
